<!-- 6 ▸ BELIEF 2 · THE STIFFNESS LOOP -->
<section id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="center"><span class="eyebrow">Why relief never lasted</span></div>
    <h2>Stiff knees get stuck in <em>a loop.</em></h2>
    <p class="lede">The knee has almost no muscle around it to keep itself warm and moving. So when it hurts, a cycle starts — and quick fixes only pause it.</p>
    <div class="split">
      <figure class="fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 360" role="img" aria-label="The stiffness loop: a knee that hurts leads to moving less, moving less drops circulation, low circulation stiffens the joint, and a stiffer joint brings more pain — a cycle that repeats.">
          <!-- four equal stages, each arc ending in an arrow, so the cycle reads as continuous -->
          <g fill="none" stroke="#eac5a6" stroke-width="22" stroke-linecap="round">
            <path d="M243.2 86.9 A96 96 0 0 1 313.1 156.8"/>
            <path d="M313.1 203.2 A96 96 0 0 1 243.2 273.1"/>
            <path d="M196.8 273.1 A96 96 0 0 1 126.9 203.2"/>
            <path d="M126.9 156.8 A96 96 0 0 1 196.8 86.9"/>
          </g>
          <g fill="#c8500f">
            <polygon points="316.8,171.3 321.4,152.7 303.9,157.0"/>
            <polygon points="228.7,276.8 247.3,281.4 243.0,263.9"/>
            <polygon points="123.2,188.7 118.6,207.3 136.1,203.0"/>
            <polygon points="211.3,83.2 192.7,78.6 197.0,96.1"/>
          </g>
          <g font-family="Archivo,sans-serif" font-weight="700" font-size="15" fill="#141311">
            <text x="220" y="40" text-anchor="middle">Knee hurts</text>
            <text x="434" y="174" text-anchor="end">You move</text>
            <text x="434" y="192" text-anchor="end">less</text>
            <text x="220" y="336" text-anchor="middle">Circulation drops</text>
            <text x="6" y="174">Joint gets</text>
            <text x="6" y="192">stiffer</text>
          </g>
          <g fill="#c8500f" font-family="Archivo,sans-serif" font-weight="800" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle">
            <text x="220" y="168">THE</text>
            <text x="220" y="186">STIFFNESS</text>
            <text x="220" y="204">LOOP</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>An explanation of why short bursts of relief don't stick — not a medical diagnosis.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;font-size:24px;margin-bottom:12px">Pain → less movement → less warmth → stiffer joint → more pain.</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:12px">It's why your knees are worst in the morning, worse in winter, and seize up after sitting. The joint cools down, blood flow drops, and everything tightens.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-bottom:12px">A ten-minute heat pack interrupts the loop. Then it goes cold, and the loop closes again. To actually loosen a stiff knee, the warmth has to be <strong style="color:var(--ink)">deep, even, and repeated daily</strong> — which is exactly what nothing in your cupboard can do.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft)">You already know heat helps. You've known it for years — it's why you own the wheat bag. The problem was never the heat. It was keeping it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

